i.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-07T11:13:08Z","updated_at":"2025-02-07T11:13:08Z","body":"The [Code of Conduct](https://godotengine.org/code-of-conduct/) team has reviewed this interaction and took some moderation decisions which we want to make explicit for people involved.\r\n\r\nWe understand that @WhalesState may have been upset by some of the communication in this thread, and decided to stop their contribution. It's their prerogative and we respect that. We want to clarify that the interactions with maintainers in this thread were about trying to understand what bug this is fixing, as the PR was opened without any details. It took quite a few comments to get to a clear description of the bug, and a MRP eventually provided by another maintainer. There wasn't any bias against a specific contributor.\r\n\r\nWe do recognize that some negatively charged reaction emojis used in the discussion may have led to unnecessary friction or triggered negative emotions. We advise everyone participating in GitHub discussions (project members and external contributors alike) to be more considerate about how such reaction emojis may be interpreted.\r\n\r\nNow for the part that actually breaches the Code of Conduct: After WhalesState decided to close this PR, 3 users previously uninvolved in the discussion rallied to escalate the situation and pile onto a contributor.\r\n\r\n@Bioblaze and @sshiiden have never before interacted with the Godot repository and just came to post unconstructive comments and emojis. We decided to block these users from further commenting on Godot issues or PRs.\r\n\r\nAs for @Ughuuu, please don't join a GitHub discussion just to comment on another contributor's conduct. You should feel free to point out conduct that affects you while you're actually having the interaction. However, joining a thread you are not in to berate another user on their conduct is really not productive (if you witness an interaction that think is inappropriate, you can notify the Code of Conduct team by email). Additionally publicly suggesting that another contributor should apologize is really over the line. Consider this a formal warning from the CoC team.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe Code of Conduct team can be contacted via conduct@godotengine.org if anyone wishes to discuss this further.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2642620004/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]